---
name: Register map to YAML
format: yaml
reverse: register-map
struct_name: demoFpgaRegs
---
{#-
  register-map-to-yaml.j2 — first bundled Jinja conversion template.

  Inverse of yaml_template_examples/generic/generate_md.py: reads a
  register-map Markdown document
    Offset | Word | Name | Size | Format | Access | Description
  and re-emits the *_fpga_types.yaml type definitions.

  Both document styles are supported:
  - one continuous table with the description + nested field/enum table
    INSIDE the Description cell (demo_fpga_types.md);
  - each register as a single pipe row (a lone line, with bare "|"
    separator lines), followed by a prose description and the nested
    field/enum table as separate lines (pab1_fpga_types.md).
  row_doc(r) / row_subrows(r) work for both styles.

  Context (TypeScript backend, see docs/reference/jinja.md):
    source   basename of the opened Markdown document
    rows     register rows in document order
             (r.Offset, r.Word, r.Name, r.Size, r.Format, r.Access, r.Description)
    params   front-matter keys of this template (struct_name, ...)

  Conversion notes (what the Markdown document knows and what it does not):
  - enum values are emitted as the numbers shown in the table
    (generate_md.py prints 0x100 as 256 — the value is the same).
  - a bitfield's padding row appears as "reserved" in the table, so the
    field name is reconstructed as <register>_padding with doc "N/A".
  - the original codegen block is not present in the table; the constant
    snake_case block below is emitted for every register — edit or delete
    it if your project uses different codegen settings.
  - the struct (params.struct_name) collects all registers in document
    order; remove the struct_name front-matter line to skip it.
-#}
# Regenerated from {{ source }} by register-map-to-yaml.j2
types:
{%- for r in rows %}
# @register {{ r.Name }}
  {{ r.Name }}:
{%- if r.Format == 'array' %}
    size: calc
    format: array
    bit_width: {{ r.Description | array_info.bit_width }}
    length: {{ r.Description | array_info.length }}
    doc: {{ r | row_doc | yaml_q }}
    fpga:
      flags: [{{ r.Access | access_flags | join(', ') }}]
{%- elif r.Format == 'enum' %}
    size: {{ r.Size | size_bits }}
    format: enum
    doc: {{ r | row_doc | yaml_q }}
    values:
{%- for v in r | row_subrows %}
      {{ v[1] }}: {{ v[0] }}
{%- endfor %}
    fpga:
      flags: [{{ r.Access | access_flags | join(', ') }}]
{%- elif r.Format == 'bitfield' %}
    size: {{ r.Size | size_bits }}
    format: bitfield
    doc: {{ r | row_doc | yaml_q }}
    fields:
{%- for f in r | row_subrows %}
{%- if f[1] == 'reserved' %}
      {{ r.Name }}_padding:
        size: {{ f[2] | size_bits }}
        doc: "N/A"
{%- else %}
      {{ f[1] }}:
        size: {{ f[2] | size_bits }}
        doc: {{ f[4] | default('N/A') | yaml_q }}
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
    fpga:
      flags: [{{ r.Access | access_flags | join(', ') }}]
{%- else %}
    size: {{ r.Size | size_bits }}
    format: {{ r.Format }}
    doc: {{ r | row_doc | yaml_q }}
    fpga:
      flags: [{{ r.Access | access_flags | join(', ') }}]
{%- endif %}
    codegen:
      c:
        naming: snake_case
{%- endfor %}
{%- if params.struct_name %}
# @register {{ params.struct_name }}
  {{ params.struct_name }}:
    format: struct
    fields:
{%- for r in rows %}
      {{ r.Name }}: EXT__{{ r.Name }}
{%- endfor %}
    codegen:
      c:
        naming: snake_case
{%- endif %}
